{"text": "Kyle Hicks Fortson\nmn\n\nEmployment\n\nSenate Health, Education, Labor and Pensions Committee\nLabor Policy Director 2010 to Present\ne Serving Chairman Lamar Alexander (2013-present) and Ranking Member Mike\nEnzi (2010-2012), respectively.\ne Direct and formulate labor and employment policy on behalf of Republican leader\nand members.\ne Supervise staff to ensure complete coverage of labor and employment issues and\nencourage professional growth.\ne Specific responsibilities include overseeing the Senate confirmation process for\nlabor nominees, hearing preparations, drafting and negotiating legislation with\nRepublican and Democrat Senate staff, staffing Senator Alexander as he manages\nfloor activity on labor issues, advising the Chairman about appropriate committee\ngoals and mapping strategies to achieve those goals.\n\nSenate Health, Education, Labor and Pensions Committee, Senator Mike Enzi,\nRanking Member (Senator Judd Gregg was Chairman during 2004 employment)\nLabor Counsel 2004-2010\ne Provided counsel, research and analysis for all labor and employment issues\narising in the HELP Committee and on the Senate floor; and assisted Senator Enzi\nand others in floor debates.\ne Organized hearings, screened and prepared witnesses for hearings, briefed other\nHELP members on hearing topics and guided legislation through mark-ups.\ne Maintained communication with Department of Labor, Senate leadership, the\nHouse of Representatives, and outside groups about the Committee\u2019s agenda.\n\u00a2 Accomplishments included attaching small business tax relief package to\nlegislation which increased the minimum wage, and negotiation and drafting of\nbipartisan mine safety legislation enacted in 2007.\n\nSenate Republican Policy Committee, Senator Jon Kyl, Chairman\nPolicy Analyst and Counsel 2003-2004\n\u00a2 Responsibilities included establishing and substantiating policy agendas for the\nissues of Pensions, Labor, Education and Welfare, as well as prioritizing and\nstrategizing to achieve that agenda.\ne Wrote policy papers to explain and promote legislative priorities to both Senators\nand staff, conducted staff briefings on upcoming legislative issues, monitored\ncommittee and floor activities and informed staff of the substance and\nimplications of every bill and amendment relating to issue areas.\n\nSenator Tim Hutchinson, Counsel 10/01-1/03\ne Advised Senator on Health, Education, Labor and Pensions Committee issues\ninvolving labor and pension policy. Also counseled Senator on bankruptcy\nreform, trade, judiciary, homeland security and campaign finance reform issues.\ne Achievements included successfully negotiating agreement creating additional\nfederal penalties for acts of eco-terrorism, and introducing Republican versions of\npension reform legislation and welfare reauthorization legislation.",
